% (notes in notes/lit-recheck-2026-10-29/). Fields that could not be established are omitted.
% The note field starts with the verification status:
%   verified-on-page, held-locally, verified-online (= "verified 2026-10-29" in REFERENCES.md: bibliographic
%   details checked online, passages not checked), best-match-unconfirmed (likely paper, not confirmed as the
%   one meant), or from-memory (check before external sharing). bibmd.py reads the status as [a-z-]+, so the
%   date goes in the rest of the note. An entry that is both held locally and checked online keeps held-locally
%   (or verified-on-page) and says "details verified online 2026-10-29" in the note.
% Keys are fixed (book/cite.py matches them; book/test_*.py pin the key set and the count of 134). Keys keep
% their original years even where a correction changed the year (barandes2023correspondence, barandes2025isp).

